{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.md","line":475,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex#thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#def:pet-ch7-busemann-function]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","line":800,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Cheeger--Gromoll splitting theorem]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0315,petersen:page-0318,petersen:page-0319}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic, thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle, thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.3.5}\n  If $(M,g)$ contains a line and has $\\Ric\\ge0$, then $(M,g)$ is isometric to\n  a product $(H\\times\\mathbb{R},\\,g_0+dt^2)$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem,lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic,thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle,thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity,prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants,def:pet-ch7-busemann-function,prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace}\n  \\sketch\n  For a line \\(c\\), \\cref{lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic} makes \\(b^++b^-\\) superharmonic; it is nonnegative and vanishes on \\(c\\), so the maximum principle makes it zero. Thus each function is weakly harmonic. Support inequalities give \\(|\\nabla b^\\pm|=1\\), and \\cref{thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity} makes them smooth. The trace identity with \\(\\Delta b^+=0\\) forces \\(\\Hess b^+=0\\), yielding \\(H\\times\\mathbb R\\).\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Cheeger--Gromoll splitting theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368372d73706c697474696e672d7468656f72656d\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0315, petersen:page-0318, petersen:page-0319</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic\">↗ lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-harmonic-regularity\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:7.3.5</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> contains a line and has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge 0$\">$\\Ric \\ge 0$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is isometric to a product <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(H\\times \\mathbb {R},\\, g_0+dt^2)$\">$(H\\times \\mathbb {R},\\, g_0+dt^2)$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-splitting-theorem\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic\">↗ lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-harmonic-regularity\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23prop%3Apet-ch7-busemann-approximants\">↗ prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23def%3Apet-ch7-busemann-function\">↗ def:pet-ch7-busemann-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23prop%3Apet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace\">↗ prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace</a> \\sketch For a line <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span>, <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368372d627573656d616e6e2d73757065726861726d6f6e6963\">item 2</a> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b^++b^-$\">$b^++b^-$</span> superharmonic; it is nonnegative and vanishes on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span>, so the maximum principle makes it zero. Thus each function is weakly harmonic. Support inequalities give <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\nabla b^\\pm |=1$\">$|\\nabla b^\\pm |=1$</span>, and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-harmonic-regularity\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368372d6861726d6f6e69632d726567756c6172697479\">item 3</a> makes them smooth. The trace identity with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta b^+=0$\">$\\Delta b^+=0$</span> forces <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Hess b^+=0$\">$\\Hess b^+=0$</span>, yielding <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H\\times \\mathbb R$\">$H\\times \\mathbb R$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#cor:pet-ch7-no-ricci-flat-sphere-product","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic","title":"lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic","label":"lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle","title":"thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle","label":"thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity","title":"thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity","label":"thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants","title":"prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants","label":"prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#def:pet-ch7-busemann-function","title":"def:pet-ch7-busemann-function","label":"def:pet-ch7-busemann-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace","title":"prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace","label":"prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#cor:pet-ch7-no-ricci-flat-sphere-product","title":"cor:pet-ch7-no-ricci-flat-sphere-product","label":"cor:pet-ch7-no-ricci-flat-sphere-product"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-structure-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-structure-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch7-structure-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-homogeneous-splitting","title":"thm:pet-ch7-homogeneous-splitting","label":"thm:pet-ch7-homogeneous-splitting"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Cheeger--Gromoll splitting theorem]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0315,petersen:page-0318,petersen:page-0319}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic, thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle, thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.3.5}\n  If $(M,g)$ contains a line and has $\\Ric\\ge0$, then $(M,g)$ is isometric to\n  a product $(H\\times\\mathbb{R},\\,g_0+dt^2)$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch7-splitting-theorem,lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic,thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle,thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity,prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants,def:pet-ch7-busemann-function,prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace}\n  \\sketch\n  For a line \\(c\\), \\cref{lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic} makes \\(b^++b^-\\) superharmonic; it is nonnegative and vanishes on \\(c\\), so the maximum principle makes it zero. Thus each function is weakly harmonic. Support inequalities give \\(|\\nabla b^\\pm|=1\\), and \\cref{thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity} makes them smooth. The trace identity with \\(\\Delta b^+=0\\) forces \\(\\Hess b^+=0\\), yielding \\(H\\times\\mathbb R\\).\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic","title":"lem:pet-ch7-busemann-superharmonic","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle","title":"thm:pet-ch7-strong-maximum-principle","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity","title":"thm:pet-ch7-harmonic-regularity","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants","title":"prop:pet-ch7-busemann-approximants","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#def:pet-ch7-busemann-function","title":"def:pet-ch7-busemann-function","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace","title":"prop:pet-ch7-volume-form-laplacian-trace","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}